>>> Qwen:

**Methods:** Researchers engineered an autonomous AI agent using GPT-4 integrated with multimodal oncology tools (vision transformers for histopathology biomarker prediction, MedSAM for radiology segmentation, web search, OncoKB, and a calculator) alongside retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) indexing ~6,800 clinical guidelines. The system was tested on 20 simulated, multimodal oncology cases requiring multi-step clinical reasoning.

**Key Result:** The agent autonomously selected appropriate tools with 87.5% accuracy, reached correct clinical conclusions in 91.0% of cases, and accurately cited guidelines 75.5% of the time. Compared to standalone GPT-4, tool integration drastically improved response completeness and accuracy from 30.3% to 87.2%.

**Limitation:** Evaluation relied on only 20 manually crafted, simulated patient cases rather than real-world clinical data, restricting generalizability and necessitating larger-scale, prospective validation before clinical deployment.


